  "assumptions": [
    "The model holds electricity use at existing sites constant through 2035. All changes shown come from new projects in the tracker.",
    "MW and electricity use follow the same scenario. Without a source schedule, the share of capacity in use rises from 20 to 100 percent over five years, following EPRI. A source date for full operation takes precedence. The load factor describes how much of this capacity is used on average over a year.",
    "Norway starts from measured electricity use published by NVE. Sweden starts between the total reported to the EU and an older RISE estimate. Finland uses its latest EU figure, from 2024. It is too low to cover all sites.",
    "EU figures include only sites that reported. Sweden had 6 reporting sites in 2023, 10 in 2024 and 71 in 2025. More reports do not tell us how much electricity use grew. Reporting covers sites with at least 500 kW of installed IT capacity, the power available to their servers and network equipment.",
    "The Norwegian figures differ because they cover businesses registered under different industry codes. NVE also includes datacentres found under other codes. Neither Norwegian series separates cryptocurrency mining.",
    "Projects without a capacity figure are missing from the modelled totals. Historical sources also differ in which sites they cover. The scenarios show what follows from these assumptions."
  ],
